      "unit_number": 2,
      "section_number": "2.1",
      "section_title": "Maximum Height and Range of Projectile",
      "content": "For a projectile launched with initial velocity v0 at an angle theta to the horizontal, the maximum height H reached is given by H = (v0^2 * sin^2(theta)) / (2 * g). The horizontal range R is given by R = (v0^2 * sin(2 * theta)) / g. The calculation begins on page 34 and concludes on page 35.",
